YM3812-LLE: the sample without shifting a negative number

The sample is the mantissa of the shifter, centred on 512, scaled by the
exponent. It is scaled with a left shift, and the shift of a negative number
is undefined behaviour, which UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program
at:

  src/chips/ym3812_lle/nopl2.c:106:41: runtime error: left shift of negative
  value -512

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The value stays within
an int: the mantissa gives -512 to 511, the shift is at most 6, and the
product -32768 to 32704.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/ym3812_lle/nopl2.c b/src/chips/ym3812_lle/nopl2.c
index f9d4715..81cde32 100644
--- a/src/chips/ym3812_lle/nopl2.c
+++ b/src/chips/ym3812_lle/nopl2.c
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ static void nopl2_cycle(nopl2_t *chip)
                 if (shift)
                 {
                     shift--;
-                    chip->sample = mant << shift;
+                    chip->sample = mant * (1 << shift);
                 }
             }
 
